<title>USA: First Northern extends stock buyback plan.</title>
<headline>First Northern extends stock buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>GREEN BAY, Wis. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Northern Capital Corp said Monday it will extend its stock repurchase program, originally scheduled to expire April 17, until Ocober 17.</p>
<p>The bank holding company said the Wisconsin Department of Financial Institutions approved the six-month extension, which will involve 219,057 common shares.</p>
<p>First Northern is the parent of First Northern Savings Bank, which operates 20 branch offices in northeastern Wisconsin and has assets of $617.9 million.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
